ScummVM Rockbox support starts with a descriptor launcher.

Create a file ending in `.scummvm`:

    gameid=sky
    engine=sky
    path=/ScummVM/sky
    savepath=/.rockbox/scummvm/saves/sky

Open that descriptor from Files. The current plugin validates the descriptor
and game data path, then runs the Rockbox backend shell.
If `path` is omitted, the launcher tries `/ScummVM/<gameid>`.

Shared engine data goes in `/.rockbox/scummvm/engine-data`. For Sky, full
gameplay requires `sky.cpt` there or in the game data directory. The intro
resource path can run from `sky.dsk`/`sky.dnr` alone, but the script/scene loop
needs the compact tables from `sky.cpt`. The plugin now parses and validates
the `sky.cpt` compact metadata during Sky preparation and section bootstrap.

Current engine state:

- `sky`: loads `sky.dnr`/`sky.dsk`, decodes resources through the imported
  ScummVM 1.9.0 RNC decoder, and renders the first static intro
  screen/palette resources (`60110`/`60111`, `60112`/`60113`,
  `60114`/`60115`) when available. It also applies the first floppy intro
  animation sequences (`60082` through `60086`) with a small native
  skip/run sequence player, then validates the section-0 fixed items and all
  grid resources (`60000` through `60069`) needed before the first playable
  scene. It also validates and retains the `sky.cpt` compact table format,
  initializes the native Sky runtime variables, and scans/steps active logic
  lists from the retained compacts. The runtime loads Sky script modules from
  `sky.dsk`, decodes core script opcodes, handles a broad set of native Sky
  mcodes, composites draw-list sprites with sorted ordering and vertical
  walk-behind masks, autosaves native runtime state, and renders decoded
  Huffman text as in-scene Sky text sprites for speech, chooser, and
  text-module events. It also drives walk-grid autoroute, dynamic grid
  mutation, collision waits, mini-bump scripts, route animation frames,
  turn tables, chooser hit-testing, CD speech playback, and upstream-mapped
  Sky SFX through the Rockbox PCM mixer path. Music start/stop mcodes can
  stream optional Sky digital music tracks named like ScummVM's enhancement
  files (`music_001.wav`, `music_104.wav`) from the game directory when they
  are 8-48 kHz PCM WAV, mixing them under speech and effects on the same
  playback channel. Native AdLib/GM/MT-32 sequencing remains unported.
- `queen`: validates `queen.1`/`queen.1c`, known retail/demo resource
  versions, and the Queen resource index. Rebuilt `QTBL` bundles are read
  directly, the English DOS floppy table uses the upstream built-in count, and
  other original releases require `queen.tbl` beside the game data. Indexed
  releases also verify that `QUEEN.JAS` exists and, for DOS versions, matches
  the expected embedded version string before the engine is marked ready. The
  native Queen loader can now resolve and read named resources through the
  index, including the built-in English DOS floppy JAS entries. The native
  runtime renders PCX/BBK room scenes, static and animated room objects,
  furniture, actors, and Joe with standing/walking BBK banks; handles default
  verbs, command batches, object/item/area/game-state mutation, entry-object
  room transitions, walk-off targets, wrong-action Joe responses, autosave
  state, four-slot inventory overlay/clicks, and core Joe walking/facing. It
  also verifies `.CUT`/`.DOG` resources referenced by native description text,
  decodes their script strings with inline speak-control token cleanup and
  simple Joe face/move control application, preserves cutaway frame/flip
  overrides across autosave restore, surfaces cutaway credit markers, previews
  cutaway/dialog metadata and first dialog options through the Rockbox overlay,
  persists first-level dialog option clicks, surfaces immediate and repeat NPC
  replies plus child options,
  auto-finishes exit-only dialog states, scans cutaway object records, applies
  current-room cutaway person-list visibility,
  applies current-room non-Joe person-record placement/move effects, applies
  simple cutaway face commands, normalizes cutaway room-fade objects to Joe,
  applies conservative cutaway animation-packet frame/flip/position/move/off-state
  effects, applies native object-level cutaway special-move state effects,
  dispatches first-click default actions, walks Joe to backdrop clicks, scans
  multi-row command matches like upstream, applies special walk-area Joe
  responses and cutaway triggers for the upstream handled rooms, supports
  explicit Queen verb cycling from the clickwheel/cancel controls with the
  selected verb shown in the overlay, supports paged four-slot inventory
  browsing from the inventory panel, supports inventory item selection with
  `USE`/`GIVE` item-on-object command dispatch, applies `.DOG` post-dialog
  inventory/cutaway triggers, follows bounded cutaway/dialog handoff chains,
  and hands cutaway `.DOG` talk files back to the dialog path.

The shell owns the screen/input loop and provides the boundary where the full
trimmed engine loop is being connected. Sky still needs native AdLib/GM/MT-32
music sequencing parity. Queen still needs full native cutaway/dialog script
execution and broader scene-loop parity beyond the currently handled command,
room, inventory, render, and metadata paths.

See docs/scummvm-rockbox-port.md for the port contract.
